SCOPE NOTE — what this license covers (and what it does not).

1. This license covers the original files of this repository
   (GDevelop-Unlocked): the patch stack and tooling under `patches/`,
   `scripts/`, `launcher/`, `packages/`, `tests/`, `web-userscript/`,
   `docs/`, and the repository's own documentation and workflows.
   `package.json` names this same license (`"license": "MIT"`).

2. Upstream GDevelop is NOT vendored in this repository. Release and
   test flows apply the patch stack onto a stock upstream checkout
   pinned in `UPSTREAM_BASELINE.json` (never committed under `review/`).
   Upstream files remain under their own licenses: the Core library,
   the game engine (GDJS), the new IDE, and all extensions (respectively
   the `Core`, `GDJS`, `newIDE` and `Extensions` folders) are under the
   MIT license; the name "GDevelop" and its logo are the exclusive
   property of Florian Rival. See `LICENSE.md` in the upstream
   checkout (root and per-folder) for the full texts. Verified against
   upstream commit `8301cdcaa4` (see `UPSTREAM_BASELINE.json`).

3. Files under `patches/` are transformation instructions (unified
   diffs) that reference upstream files; they are this repository's
   original work and are covered by this license. They do not reproduce
   upstream sources.
